        "description": "Give file (its name in the person's files, such as /Projects/sample-card.pdf, or its identity); printer (from tool:printers; the computer's default when left out), copies, paper (the print system's size name, such as Letter, A4, Tabloid), fit (true to fit the page), sides (one-sided, two-sided-long-edge), color (color or monochrome), orientation and title when wanted. Returns printed, the printer, the job id and said. Large-format or many copies belong to a print shop (workflow:print-and-deliver).",
        "input_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "file"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "file": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1
            },
            "printer": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "copies": {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 1,
              "maximum": 100
            },
            "paper": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "fit": {
              "type": "boolean"
            },
            "sides": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "color": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "orientation": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "title": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "stored": {
              "type": "object",
              "description": "What this run reads of the person's own things, read by the caller from where the person keeps them (the engine keeps none) and given here: files: {name: text or {base64}} under /, as this row's `stored` lists. What is not given is not there."
            }
          }
        },
        "output_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "printed",
            "said"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "printed": {
              "type": "boolean"
            },
            "printer": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "job": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "said": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        },
        "invoke": {
          "kind": "computer",
          "capabilities": [
            "use-the-print-system"
          ],
          "workdir": "/opt/print-here",
          "stdout": "json",
          "argv": [
            "node",
            "/opt/workflows/do-work/run-a-function.mjs",
            "/opt/print-here/read-data/print-here.mjs",
            "print"
          ],
          "stdin": {
            "fill": {
              "from": "input"
            }
          },
          "files": {
            "package_files": [
              {
                "package": "print-here",
                "paths": [
                  "read-data"
                ],
                "at": "/opt/print-here"
              },
              {
                "package": "workflows",
                "paths": [
                  "do-work/run-a-function.mjs",
                  "read-data/host-actions.mjs"
                ],
                "at": "/opt/workflows"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "result_selector": "$.result",
        "verify": [
          {
            "kind": "sample-run",
            "input": {},
            "laid_files": [
              {
                "path": "/opt/print-here/read-data/print-here.json",
                "text": "{\"_what\":\"Printing on the person's own printers from their Mac (read-data/print-here.mjs: `printers` and `print`). A file is read from the person's files by its name or identity, by the run's host action (`host.readWholeFile`), and handed to the Mac's print system on standard input, so nothing is written to a folder first. `commands` are the Mac's own print commands with their arguments: `list` reads the printers and the default, `print` sends one job, where {printer}, {copies} and {title} are filled from the input. `options` maps each input field a person may give to the print system's own option name (paper size, fit to page, two-sided, colour); an option whose value was not given is left out. `read_bytes` is how much one read asks for. `most_bytes` is the largest file sent. A host that hands runs over by id journals each job before it is sent (`may_have_started` is said when one may already be at the printer). A new option is a row.\",\"commands\":{\"list\":[\"/usr/bin/lpstat\",\"-p\",\"-d\"],\"print\":[\"/usr/bin/lp\",\"-d\",\"{printer}\",\"-n\",\"{copies}\",\"-t\",\"{title}\"]},\"options\":{\"paper\":\"media\",\"fit\":\"fit-to-page\",\"sides\":\"sides\",\"color\":\"print-color-mode\",\"orientation\":\"orientation-requested\"},\"read_bytes\":262144,\"most_bytes\":100000000,\"default_title\":\"Print job\",\"words\":{\"printed\":\"Sent {title} to {printer} ({copies} copy).\",\"no_printer\":\"This Mac has no printer set up. Add one in System Settings > Printers & Scanners, or use a print shop.\",\"unknown_printer\":\"This Mac has no printer named {printer}. Its printers: {printers}.\",\"no_file\":\"Say which file to print: its name in your files or its identity.\",\"which_printer\":\"Say which printer to use: this Mac has no default printer. Its printers: {printers}.\",\"too_big\":\"{title} is {mb} MB, larger than this Mac sends to a printer ({most} MB). Use a print shop.\",\"not_read\":\"Could not read {file} from your files: {error}\",\"may_have_started\":\"This print job may already have started. Check the printer before trying again.\"}}"
              }
            ],
            "stand_in_programs": {
              "lpstat": "printf 'printer sample-printer is idle.  enabled since Mon 01 Jan 2026 00:00:00 UTC\\n'\nprintf 'system default destination: sample-printer\\n'",
              "lp": "cat > /dev/null\necho \"request id is sample-printer-1 (1 file(s))\""
            }
          }
        ],
        "stored": [
          {
            "files": "/",
            "operations": [
              "find_file",
              "read_file"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
